<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Sánchez of Gascony</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 997</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Sánchez was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a> from about 961 until about 997. He defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> raiders, traditionally at the Battle of Taller around 982, founded the abbey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-sever">Saint-Sever</a> in 988 and, after inheriting the county of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bordeaux">Bordeaux</a>, made it the ducal seat. Through his marriage to Urraca of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> he had close ties with the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamplona">Pamplona</a>.</p></div>
